            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "using concrete object paths in the example could help. I'm also confused because `Fru0` is removed but the `GetSubTree` did not return it in the first place?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 15,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Willy Tu",
                        "email": "wltu@google.com",
                        "username": "wltu"
                    },
                    "message": "tried to updated it a bit more to be more clear. Please do let me know if it is still not clear enough.\n\nThe issue is `/xyz/openbmc_project/FruDevice/Fru` get return in `GetSubTree`, but by the time that entity-manager is making the GetAll on the output of `GetSubTree`... it got removed. It is a race condition."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "```suggestion\n- Entity Manager calls GetAll on Fru_1 and failed, resulting in Fru_1\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Willy Tu",
                        "email": "wltu@google.com",
                        "username": "wltu"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "nit (unrelated)\n\n```suggestion\nJan 20 00:25:02 bmc entity-manager[22410]: error calling GetAll on  xyz.openbmc_project.FruDevice /xyz/openbmc_project/FruDevice/Fru_1 xyz.openbmc_project.FruDevice\n```\n\nlog statement also needs fixing, `getall` is confusing when it's actually `GetAll` function. Things like that make it hard to search logs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Willy Tu",
                        "email": "wltu@google.com",
                        "username": "wltu"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device/fru_device.cpp",
                    "line": 899,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "function size has increased, can you extract something, possibly in a preceding patch? This new change is not making the code any simpler. See core guidelines for recommendation on function size.\n\nI would recommend a separate function to compute `productName`."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/fru_device/fru_device.cpp",
                    "line": 899,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Willy Tu",
                        "email": "wltu@google.com",
                        "username": "wltu"
                    },
                    "message": "sure, will clean it up in another patch."
                }
